data: {"type": "text_delta_finish", "role": "text", "content": "To set up **RCS messaging (for rich messaging)** in Gupshup\u2019s ecosystem, the documentation centers on **RCS Agent onboarding in Dotgo RBM Hub** (this is the prerequisite that enables rich messaging capabilities).\n\n### Setup (from the KB)\n1. **Register as an RCS Agent (RBM Hub / Dotgo)**\n   - Submit your **agent/brand metadata** (agent name, summary, privacy policy & terms URLs, supported languages, agent message type, business/brand details, etc.).\n2. **Create/prepare your messaging templates (as applicable)**\n   - The docs indicate you\u2019ll need to have templates approved/available as part of RCS messaging readiness.\n3. **Configure authentication (OAuth2)**\n   - Set up **OAuth2** using **client credentials** (per the KB guidance).\n4. **Implement message sending**\n   - Use the documented sending/API approach to deliver RCS messages.\n5. **Set up webhooks**\n   - Configure webhooks to receive **incoming messages** and **delivery/callback** events.\n\n### Important note about your wording (\u201cfor my WhatsApp account\u201d)\nThe KB content I found describes **RCS agent onboarding and enablement** via **Dotgo RBM Hub / Gupshup Channels**, but it does not clearly spell out a step like \u201cconnect your WhatsApp account\u201d in those same terms.\n\n**Could you clarify what you mean by \u201cWhatsApp account\u201d here\u2014are you trying to connect an existing _WhatsApp Business Platform_ number, or are you onboarding an _RCS agent/brand_ to send RCS rich messages via Dotgo?**"}

