data: {"type": "text_delta_finish", "role": "text", "content": "We don\u2019t have specific documentation available in this chat environment for **API node error handling in Bot Studio**, so I can\u2019t give you an exact \u201cclick here\u201d setup for the **API Node**.\n\nWhat I *can* suggest (common Bot Studio pattern) is to handle API failures explicitly in your flow instead of relying on automatic error behavior:\n\n- **Add branching after the API call**: use a follow-up node that checks the API response (or an HTTP status field, if your setup exposes one) and routes to:\n  - **Success path** (parse/consume response)\n  - **Failure path** (fallback message, retry logic, or logging)\n- **Create a safe fallback response**: on failure, set a variable like `error_message` / `api_status` and return a user-friendly message (avoid showing raw error payloads).\n- **Guard JSON parsing**: if the API response is not guaranteed to be valid JSON on errors, ensure your JSON handling is only executed on the success branch.\n\nCould you clarify\u2014are you trying to handle **(1) non-200 HTTP status codes**, **(2) timeouts/network failures**, or **(3) JSON parsing errors** after a successful HTTP call?"}

